uddles, and lighting.\n- All collectible dollar coins.\n- Course geometry, camera logic, controls, collisions, hearts, and HUD.\n- The Screen 07-to-08 deep descent.\n- All Blender \".blend\" files and Blender Python scripts.\n- The Three.js and TypeScript game.\n- The Android Capacitor project and APK.\n- Playwright screenshots, tests, and comparison files.\n- Google Flow cinematic integration code.\n- World Labs Atlas/Marble reference preparation and import utilities.\n- All saved design prompts, project instructions, conversation archives, agent logs, and recovery reports.\n\nRun Git LFS retrieval and integrity checks.\n\nDo not leave small placeholder files in place of the real 3D assets.\n\nCheck the project manifest and identify anything that cannot be recovered.\n\n3. RESTORE ALL TEN SPECIALIST DESIGN AGENTS\n\nMy existing specialist agents are saved in:\n\n\".claude/agents/\"\n\nRestore the existing configurations for:\n\n1. Reference Match Director\n2. Benny Character Artist\n3. Cartoon Girl Character Artist\n4. Washer Environment Modeler\n5. Water FX Specialist\n6. Foam and Bubble Specialist\n7. Path and Camera Transition Engineer\n8. Animation and Gameplay Engineer\n9. Playwright Visual QA Specialist\n10. Android Build and Performance Specialist\n\nRead the saved instructions, transcripts, outputs, and task notes for every agent.\n\nThese agents have already completed substantial work.\n\nDo not recreate their designs or discard their saved progress.\n\nLive agents from the old account cannot automatically transfer, so restart the necessary agents from their saved configurations and last committed work.\n\nAssign each specialist clearly separated file ownership to avoid conflicting edits.\n\n4. RESUME EXACTLY WHERE SCREEN 05 STOPPED\n\nMy previous Claude account was working on:\n\n05 · FLOW INTO THE CURRENT\n\nFour main specialists were working on:\n\n- Walls, gold rings, and tunnel glow.\n- The winding cyan-and-pink river.\n- Foam, bubbles, and water splashes.\n- Benny's proportions.\n\nThe Foam and Bubble Specialist reported finishing its assigned task.\n\nIts improvements include replacing the unnatural white spikes underneath Benny with a softer spray fan and arranging foam into continuous banks.\n\nHowever, its measurements showed that the near-camera foam banks were approximately 49% and 44% of the image width, compared with about 18% and 15% in the approved reference.\n\nCorrect this excess foam coverage while preserving the improved spray effects.\n\nThe specialist also reported approximately 19 large and 12 small bubbles.\n\nThe other specialists were still modifying their assigned files when the old account reached its limit.\n\nInspect the latest commits, source files, and specialist transcripts to determine their exact saved states.\n\nDo not redo their work unnecessarily.\n\nRestart unfinished specialists and continue from the actual saved changes.\n\n5. MY APPROVED SCREEN 05 IS THE VISUAL TARGET\n\nThe current game is playable, but the artwork is still not close enough to my approved image.\n\nMy approved Screen 05 includes:\n\nTunnel\n\nDeep glossy violet and magenta metallic walls, dark oval perforations, evenly spaced reflective yellow-gold rings, small gold wall fittings, and a long tunnel reaching a distant warm light.\n\nWater\n\nA wide, thick electric-cyan current with beautiful sweeping hot-pink S-shaped ribbons, glossy blue-white reflections, realistic-looking moving water, foam banks, and iridescent bubbles.\n\nBenny\n\nA round, fluffy pink character, purple-and-white striped knitted beanie, purple pom-pom, correctly positioned gold star, and appropriately sized hat and body.\n\nCollectibles\n\nRich reflective gold dollar coins with embossed upright \"$\" symbols and detailed ridged rims, following the winding cyan water.\n\nCamera\n\nThird-person view, behind and slightly above Benny, showing a dramatic winding river extending deeply into the washer tunnel.\n\nFIX THESE REMAINING ISSUES\n\n- The water looks too much like a flat blue road.\n- The pink water bands need stronger continuous S-shaped curves.\n- The tunnel walls are still too bright and pink-orange.\n- The gold rings need better color, reflectivity, and depth.\n- The distant yellow-orange glow is too large.\n- Some foam banks are too wide.\n- Benny's proportions still need reference matching.\n- The coins must follow the river with correct size, spacing, and perspective.\n- The entire image needs richer depth, more polished materials, and better lighting.\n\nDo not replace my approved design with another creative interpretation.\n\nUse the existing real 3D scene and improve it.\n\n6. RESTORE BLENDER AND THE 3D ENVIRONMENT\n\nMy previous account used Blender 5.3.0 in headless mode.\n\nRestore the existing installation scripts and verify Blender.\n\nInspect the saved Screen 05 Blender source:\n\n\"qa/worldlabs/05/blender/screen05_layout.blend\"\n\nThis contains the reconstructed tunnel, river geometry, cyan core path, ring markers, and other layout information.\n\nUse the actual game camera and reference image to refine the 3D geometry.\n\nIf Blender MCP requires a desktop window that is unavailable in the cloud, use Blender Python scripting instead.\n\nDo not report that Blender MCP works unless you have verified it.\n\nUse Blender to improve the environment rather than creating another unrelated prototype.\n\n7. RESTORE WORLD LABS ATLAS AND MARBLE WORKFLOWS\n\nMy previous Claude account installed the official World Labs plugin.\n\nCheck whether this new account has the plugin installed.\n\nRestore its supported setup and inspect the available World Labs skills and MCP servers.\n\nWorld Labs Atlas\n\nThe hosted MCP endpoint is:\n\n\"https://api.atlas.worldlabs.ai/mcp\"\n\nCheck whether my current Claude account has an authenticated Atlas connector.\n\nIf the connector is missing, explain how to reconnect it securely.\n\nIf authorization works, run the free read-only \"list_projects\" check.\n\nDo not spend paid Atlas credits without my permission.\n\nIf Atlas reports that I have no active account, tell me clearly and continue with Blender.\n\nWorld Labs Marble\n\nMarble is a separate website service:\n\n\"https://marble.worldlabs.ai\"\n\nI may create my Screen 05 environment myself on Marble and export it.\n\nRestore our saved Marble preparation files:\n\n\"qa/worldlabs/05/geometry_ref/\"\n\n\"qa/worldlabs/05/MARBLE_MANUAL.md\"\n\nRestore the existing Blender import and measurement tool for Marble/Atlas exports.\n\nDo not reuse rejected background reconstructions with rectangular patches, ghost artifacts, or invented water.\n\nWhen I provide a Marble \".glb\", \".ply\", or another supported export, use Blender to import, measure, and compare it with our existing washer tunnel.\n\nUse only geometry that improves the approved design.\n\nDo not replace real gameplay with static splats or videos.\n\nOther asset-generation tools\n\nCheck the availability of Meshy MCP and Hyper3D Rodin.\n\nReconnect them only through supported account authorization.\n\nReport which tools are actually available, which require sign-in, and which would cost extra credits.\n\nDo not spend paid external credits without my explicit approval.\n\n8. RESTORE PLAYWRIGHT AND VISUAL QA\n\nVerify the Playwright MCP connection.\n\nCapture actual gameplay screenshots at Android portrait resolutions.\n\nDo not create new artwork and call it gameplay.\n\nFor Screen 05, provide:\n\n- My original approved screenshot.\n- The latest real playable 3D screenshot.\n- The previous version for comparison.\n- A side-by-side visual comparison.\n- A transparent overlay highlighting differences.\n\nKeep the camera and screenshot checkpoint consistent.\n\nFix the differences systematically.\n\nAim for approximately 90–95% visual fidelity where technically feasible, but report actual progress rather than claiming an unverified match.\n\n9. PRESERVE ALL ELEVEN SCREENS AND GAMEPLAY\n\nKeep my full Rainbow game